{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/995659-prime-sphere","id":995659,"title":"Prime Sphere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-30T09:03:57-07:00","id":995659,"title":"Prime Sphere","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using Prime 2, the mage can \u201cenergize\u201d the reality of an<br /> object so that it can inflict or soak aggravated damage. </div> </div> </div>I found this quote in How do you do that. Does that mean you can use that on a vampire to make him able to soak aggravated damage with his normal stamina or you still need matter for it? since their bodies are not &quot;living&quot; I believe they can be treated like objects and only need prime 2 or maybe 3? well yeah thats my question, is it possible?<br /> Thanks in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:40:09-07:00","id":995788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/995659-prime-sphere#post995659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found this quote in How do you do that. Does that mean you can use that on a vampire to make him able to soak aggravated damage with his normal stamina or you still need matter for it? since their bodies are not &quot;living&quot; I believe they can be treated like objects and only need prime 2 or maybe 3? well yeah thats my question, is it possible?<br /> Thanks in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No -- vampires, in this context, don't count as &quot;objects&quot;, any more than they do for most other purposes (they are not alive vis-a-vis the Life Sphere, alone, but neither are they Matter, as delineated). Prime:2 can empower an object, proper, to resist/inflict aggravated damage, or similarly do so for a given (F)orce, but not to entities/beings. (Depending on the edition/setting you're using, that requires either a conjunctional Life effect -- usually Prime:2/3, Life:3, or Prime:2/Matter:2/Life:2 for vampires... though, again, different books say different things.) Just as Prime:4 can't be used to undo a vampire as it could a properly inanimate object or force (you need Prime:5, just as you would for a properly living entity, spirit, what-have-you), neither can Prime:2, alone, empower a vampire's body the way it could a robot/sword/housefire/what-have-you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T10:45:38-07:00","id":996687,"title":"","content":"If you enchant your body with Prime 3 you can soak aggravated damage.<br /> Lethal too?<br /> The effect only mentions agg...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:22:00-07:00","id":996896,"title":"","content":"Presumably if you can soak Agg, it means Lethal is assumed.<br /> <br /> I do know that, at least in Revised, you could use Prime 3 to enchant parts of your body to <i>deal</i> aggravated as well. Made Akashics more of combat monsters than they already are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}